Embedded provider credentials (game & subtitle metadata)

To scrape game artwork and metadata out of the box, released builds may embed the
project's own registered developer credentials for the providers below, so a fresh
install works without the user creating accounts. A user who supplies their own
credentials in the addon settings always overrides the embedded ones. The embedded
values live only in git-ignored build inputs (native/secrets/) and are obfuscated in
the binary — a speed bump, not secrecy; they are revocable and re-issued per release.

Each provider's API terms govern use of these credentials:

  ScreenScraper   Registered software credentials (devid/devpassword). Anonymous use
                  runs at a shared rate limit; a user's own ScreenScraper account is
                  the optional accelerator. https://www.screenscraper.fr
  TheGamesDB      A public API key. https://thegamesdb.net
  IGDB            Twitch developer client id/secret (IGDB is a Twitch service).
                  https://www.igdb.com/api  ·  https://dev.twitch.tv
  SteamGridDB     NOT embedded — SteamGridDB issues keys per user account, so this
                  provider stays user-supplied. https://www.steamgriddb.com

Respect each provider's terms of service and rate limits when redistributing a build
that embeds credentials.
